\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For September 15\b0\par\par\uc2 2,379 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 09:13\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: JAPAN LAUNCHES \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , YEN DOWN SHARPLY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Wednesday for the first time in more than six years, launching a wave of yen selling to deal with "severe economic conditions" facing the country. (published 0438 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: BOJ NODA VOWS 'SWIFT AND DECISIVE' ACTION IF NECESSARY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A Bank of Japan policy board member said Wednesday that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will take policy steps "swiftly and decisively" if the country's economic recovery falters and its deflationary trend worsens. (published 0359 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ NODA: TO PROVIDE AMPLE FUNDS, MAKING USE OF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FUNDS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan will make use of yen sold in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , policy board member Tadao Noda said Wednesday, indicating that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may not soak up the extra \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the market. (published 0637 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN MOF OFFICIAL: USUALLY, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  INVOLVES REPEATED ACTION \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market usually involved repeated action, not one-off moves, a Japanese finance ministry official said Wednesday, suggesting the authorities are prepared to continue \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as needed to curb the yen's strength. (published 0426 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SINGAPORE WEIGHING YEN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IMPACT; JAPAN ACTION MAY HELP ASIA -SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore is gauging the impact of Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which should help other Asian authorities cope with their strong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , a person familiar with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's thinking said Wednesday. (published 0532 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PBOC ADVISER: MONETARY POLICY MUST RETURN TO NORMAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's monetary policy must return to normal, People's Bank of China adviser Xia Bin said Wednesday, adding the rapid increase in lending last year created some asset price problems. (published 0454 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA FDI GROWTH DROPS AGAIN, BUT TREND UNCLEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Growth in foreign direct investment in China slowed sharply for the second consecutive month in August, data issued Wednesday showed, but some economists said a statistical quirk played a big role and monthly fluctuations don't reflect the overall trend. (published 0555 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PBOC ADVISER: PROPERTY MARKET ADJUSTMENTS TO TAKE 2-3 YEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It will take two to three years for China's property market to complete the adjustments induced by the tightening measures introduced earlier this year to curb speculation and lower prices, People's Bank of China adviser Xia Bin said Wednesday. (published 0524 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA YUAN HITS FRESH HIGH ON WEAK DOLLAR, FIXING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  guided the yuan to another high against the U.S. dollar for the fourth consecutive trading session Wednesday, after the dollar slumped in international markets overnight and ahead of U.S. Congressional hearings on Beijing's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy. (published 0516 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA: GROUNDLESS TO SAY CHINA MANIPULATING YUAN TO BOOST TRADE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It is groundless to say China manipulates its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to boost foreign trade, Commerce Ministry spokesman Yao Jian said Wednesday at a news conference. (published 0256 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: AUSSIE CONSUMER SENTIMENT, HOUSING DISAPPOINT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Even as Australian consumer confidence dipped broadly in September, economists and markets aren't backpedaling from their view that the local economy is still booming and the central will get back to hiking interest rates. (published 0516 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: S KOREA JOBLESS RATE FALLS IN SIGN OF GROWING OPTIMISM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's unemployment rate fell significantly in August as the private sector stepped up hiring to meet growing demand from both domestic and external markets. (published 0246 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SINGAPORE 2Q UNEMPLOYMENT FLAT AT 2.2% SEASONALLY ADJ VS 1Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's unemployment rate was unchanged at 2.2% in the second quarter from the first, according to the Ministry of Manpower's final estimates released Wednesday. (published 0200 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =DATA SNAP: PHILIPPINES JOBLESS RATE EASES TO 6.9% IN JULY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The unemployment rate in the Philippines eased in July from a two-year high in April as the economy added around 930,000 jobs, mostly in agriculture, the latest jobs survey of the National Statistics Office showed Wednesday. (published 0208 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: PHILIPPINES JULY WORKERS REMITTANCE UP 8.2% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippine expatriates in July sent home $1.62 billion, an increase of 8.2% from a year earlier and nearly eclipsing the record level set in June, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Wednesday. (published 0644 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA EXIM BANK TO ISSUE 3-YEAR YUAN BONDS IN HK IN 4TH QUARTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Export-Import Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  plans to issue three-year yuan bonds in Hong Kong in the fourth quarter to meet growing local demand, bank Vice President Zhu Xinqiang said Wednesday. (published 0319 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CENTRAL HUIJIN SETS COUPON RANGES FOR BOND SALE THURSDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Central Huijin Investment Ltd., the domestic investment arm of China's sovereign-wealth fund, said Wednesday it set the indicative range for the coupons on its bond sale Thursday, which could raise as much as CNY55 billion . (published 0337 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WOOLWORTHS PRICES US$1.25B OF SENIOR NOTES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Woolworths Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday it has priced a US$1.25 billion bond issue, some of which will be used to pay off a share market buyback. (published 2357 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: JAPAN TAKES ON THE $4 TRILLION MONSTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Those working on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  desk at the Bank of Japan may find themselves selling lots and lots of yen in the next 24 hours. (published 0507 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =PREVIEW: RBI MAY LIFT INDIA RATES 25BPS AS INFLATION WEIGHS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is likely to raise its two key policy rates by 25 basis points each Thursday as it seeks to restrain inflationary expectations even as the economy continues growing strongly. (published 0617 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =PREVIEW: HK JUNE-AUGUST JOBLESS LIKELY UNCHANGED AT 4.3% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong's unemployment rate likely held steady in the three months ended Aug. 31, but economists said it could fall toward the end of the year as the city's economy continues to grow. (published 0538 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA RESOURCES GAS: TO RAISE HK$2.47 BLN VIA SHARE PLACEMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Resources Gas Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday it will raise HK$2.47 billion via a share placement to finance its acquisition of city gas-distribution businesses in China. (published 0017 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA NATIONAL BUILDING MATERIAL TO RAISE HK$3.82 BLN IN SHARE PLACEMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China National Building Material Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday it is raising HK$3.82 billion in a share placement for debt repayment and general working capital. (published 0125 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par LAS VEGAS SANDS CHAIRMAN: NO IMPETUS FOR MARINA BAY SANDS IPO RIGHT NOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Las Vegas Sands Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Chairman \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sheldon Adelson\f28 \uc2 \f2  said he sees no impetus right now to spin off the group's US$5.5 billion Singapore integrated resort in an initial public offering. (published 0154 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 THAI AIRWAYS\f28 \uc2 \f2  OFFERS NEW SHARES AT THB31 EACH, CHEAPER THAN EXPECTED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thai Airways International PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Wednesday that its offer of new shares, targeted to raise THB15 billion in fresh funds, has been priced at THB31 each, cheaper than what the market expected. (published 0440 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA PACIFIC INSURANCE JANUARY-AUGUST LIFE INSURANCE PREMIUMS CNY61.2 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Pacific Insurance Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday it collected life insurance premiums totaling CNY61.2 billion in the January-August period and property insurance premiums totaling CNY34.8 billion. (published 0013 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PING AN BOARD OKS SHENZHEN DEVELOPMENT BANK, PING AN BANK MERGER PLAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ping An Insurance Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . of China Ltd. said Wednesday its board approved a plan to merge Ping An Bank Co. and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shenzhen Development Bank Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (published 0041 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =INTERVIEW: ATIC PLANS TO INVEST $6B-$7B IN ABU DHABI CHIP PLANT-CEO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Technology investment firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Advanced Technology Investment Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . plans to spend US$6 billion-US$7 billion to build a chip manufacturing facility in Abu Dhabi, its chief executive said. (published 0322 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA: TO PAY ATTENTION TO BHP'S BID FOR POTASH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's Ministry of Commerce will pay attention to mining giant \f28 \uc2 \f2 BHP Billiton Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s bid for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Potash Corp. of Saskatchewan Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., as the deal will impact China, ministry spokesman Yao Jian said Wednesday, in the government's first comment on the issue. (published 0538 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA: THOSE RESPONSIBLE FOR SHINHAN SITUATION WILL BE HELD ACCOUNTABLE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean regulators will investigate the management turmoil at Shinhan Financial Group Co. and will hold those responsible for the situation accountable, a senior government official said Wednesday. (published 0209 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PRIME INFRASTRUCTURE REFINANCES CORPORATE FACILITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Transport and energy infrastructure fund \f28 \uc2 \f2 Prime Infrastructure Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Wednesday it has replaced its undrawn A$300 million corporate facility with a new revolving corporate facility that matures in February 2013, to be provided by suitor Canada's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brookfield Infrastructure Partners LP\f28 \uc2 \f2  . (published 0000 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TELECOM NZ: ACHIEVING GOVERNMENT OBJECTIVES WILL BE CHALLENGE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand Ministry of Economic Development said Wednesday it is releasing a discussion document outlining initial thoughts on regulatory changes that may be required if Telecom spins off its infrastructure arm to participate in a government-led NZ$3 billion broadband initiative. (published 2141 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EROS INTERNATIONAL MEDIA SETS IPO PRICE IN INR158-INR175 BAND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 15-09-10 0713GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's Eros International Media Ltd. Wednesday set its proposed initial public offering in the indicative price band of INR158-INR175, according to a newspaper advertisement. (published 0312 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOWER INSURANCE RESOLVES DISPUTES WITH ANZ NATIONAL BANK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tower Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday it has entered into an agreement that resolves its dispute with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Australia & New Zealand Banking Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . over the renewal of insurance policies. (published 2258 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA TO REQUIRE LISTED COMPANIES TO ISSUE ENVIRONMENTAL IMPACT REPORTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China plans to require listed companies in highly polluting industries to make regular environmental impact reports in a bid to improve disclosure on such matters and control pollution from heavy industries. (published 0049 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par VIET THANG AQUAFEED TO DEBUT ON BOURSE AT VND21,000 A SHARE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Viet Thang Aquafeed JSC will debut on the Hochiminh Stock Exchange on Sept. 24 at VND21,000 a share, the stock market operator said Wednesday. (published 0317 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NEWS CORP: NEWS LIMITED AGREES TO SELL FIJI TIMES FOR UNDISCLOSED SUM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 News Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s Australian arm, \f28 \uc2 \f2 News Limited\f28 \uc2 \f2 , said Tuesday it has agreed to sell its Fiji Times newspaper to Motibhai & Co., after the Fijian government issued a decree that the nation's media groups be owned by Fijian companies. (published 0520 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DRB-HICOM OFFICIAL: EXPECT TO SIGN ASSEMBLY PACT WITH VOLKSWAGEN BY YEAR END \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DRB-Hicom Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2  expects to sign a definitive agreement with German auto maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Volkswagen AG\f28 \uc2 \f2  for the assembly of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Volkswagen\f28 \uc2 \f2  vehicles in Malaysia by the end of the year, DRB-Hicom Managing Director Mohd. Khamil Jamil said Wednesday. (published 0537 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 KOOKMIN BANK\f28 \uc2 \f2  EXPECTS TO RETURN TO PROFIT IN 3Q - CEO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Kookmin swung to a second-quarter net loss of KRW346.72 billion, weighed down by heavy provisioning. Most of KB Financial's earnings come from the banking unit. (published 0620 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES MIXED; TOKYO SURGES ON YEN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stocks were mixed Wednesday while the Tokyo market staged a stunning turnaround after the yen fell sharply due to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from Japanese authorities. (published 0419 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CHINA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MINISTRY: OPPOSE US IMPORT DUTIES ON CHINA STEEL PIPE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China "resolutely opposes" a U.S. antidumping probe on Chinese steel pipe exports, Ministry of Commerce spokesman Yao Jian said at a regular briefing to reporters Wednesday. (published 0304 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: OGX EXEC: VALUE UP TO 30% OF BRAZIL ASSET AT $12B-$14B \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 OGX Petroleo e Gas\f28 \uc2 \f2  Participacoes SA is expecting to strike a deal worth $12 billion to $14 billion for a stake of up to 30% in oil discoveries it had made in Brazil's Campos Basin, an OGX official said Wednesday. (published 0534 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =CHINA ENERGY WATCH: INDIA, CHINA VIE FOR COAL MARKET SUPREMACY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As India's quest for coal heats up, the South Asian nation may need to lock horns more tightly with bigger neighbor China to secure enough of the fuel to feed its fast-expanding economy. (published 0443 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA SECRETARY: NO INFORMATION ON BARRING CHINA IN OIL, GAS BLOCKS AUCTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's oil ministry currently doesn't have any information about a reported ban on China, Pakistan and Bangladesh bidding for oil and gas blocks in India, oil secretary S. Sundareshan said Wednesday. (published 0631 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GLOBAL WHEAT TRADE VOLUME TO FALL ON BLACK SEA DROUGHT -US WHEAT ASSOCIATES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The volume of wheat traded globally will likely shrink significantly, to around 125 million metric tons in 2010-11 from 132 million tons the previous year, U.S. Wheat Associates said Wednesday. (published 0145 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA MINISTERIAL PANEL TO CONSIDER NEW MINING LAW SEPT 17 - MINISTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's new mining law will likely be considered by an inter-ministerial panel on Sept. 17, the federal mines minister said Wednesday. (published 0657 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GOLD MAY HIT $1,500 BEFORE 2010 ENDS -AMERICAN PRECIOUS METALS ADVISORS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gold prices could rise to $1,500 a troy ounce within the year and may even rise to $5,000 in the years ahead before the current price cycle reverses, American Precious Metals Advisors Managing Director Jeoffrey Nichols said Wednesday. (published 0640 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BHP BILLITON CEO: NEED TO ANTICIPATE A GLOBAL RATE FOR CARBON \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BHP Billiton Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Chief Executive \f28 \uc2 \f2 Marius Kloppers\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Wednesday that there is a need for a clear price signal on carbon emissions and urged the Australian government and businesses to anticipate changes. (published 0421 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: PAKISTAN'S LARGEST REFINERY RESTARTS; RUNS LIKELY SUBDUED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Pak Arab Refinery Ltd., known as Parco, has restarted its 100,000-barrel-a-day refinery near Multan after flooding, but throughput will likely be limited for some time as access to the plant remains restricted. (published 0618 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SHFE TO ADJUST MARGIN, TRADING LIMITS FOR HOLIDAYS SEPT. 21-OCT. 8 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Shanghai Futures Exchange said it will adjust its limits for margin trading and price volatility in all futures contracts traded on the bourse for the Mid-Autumn Festival and the National Day holidays, from Sept. 21 to Oct. 8. (published 0235 GMT) [ 15-09-10 0713GMT ]\f28 \par \par 