\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2  Record Fixing Makes JPY  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Harder\b0\par\par\uc2 148 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 September 2010\par 03:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0144 GMT [Dow Jones] \b \highlight22\uc2 China central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's record-low fixing of USD/CNY, at 6.7509, makes it harder for Japan to make a strong case that \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is needed to contain the strong JPY, says Douglas Borthwick, managing director of Faros Trading. "As China is now telegraphing they are comfortable with further CNY strength, the region's central banks will also be able to let their respective \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthen," further isolating Tokyo in its efforts to put a floor on USD/JPY, Borthwick adds. Notes Faros now looking for significant drops in USD/Asians. USD/JPY last at 84.17 vs 84.21 late Friday in NY trade. (david.roman@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 [ 13-09-10 0144GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1012 1037 1085 5011 5063 55113 55117 75112   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100913e69d0003a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
