gs season on positive note; "It's been one of those risk on again stories." Weaker equity markets across much of Asia now weighing on sentiment. Tips support to hold around 0.7080, resistance at 0.7150. Says investors interested in this week's domestic data, such as retail sales, 2Q CPI but main focus on U.S. earnings. (rebecca.howard@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0423 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/CNY stays moderately higher midday in quiet trading after higher-than-expected dollar-yuan central parity; on OTC, USD/CNY at 6.7756 vs 6.7711 last close. "Some people thought perhaps there was a typo in the central parity rate (set at 6.7802 vs 6.7718 yesterday) as many expected it would be closer to the 6.7700 level," says Shanghai-based trader at foreign bank. "It appears the recent low of CNY6.7676 could be the near-term bottom for the dollar as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times last week to defend the 6.7700 level." Adds, market participants awaiting for macroeconomic data, including 2Q GDP, Thursday. Any signs of slowing growth could stall CNY appreciation trend for time being, he says. USD/CNY tipped at 6.7650-6.7800 for session. (joy.shaw@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0418 GMT [Dow Jones] (An item at 0230 GMT misstated the index rise in the headline. The correct version follows:) Kospi trims earlier gains, now +0.2% at 1738.21 in thin trade, after Chinese stocks open lower. "Investors are not making aggressive moves today...the market is waiting to check Intel's results tonight," says \uc2 Samsung Securities\uc2 ' Chung Myoung-ji. Adds Kospi may break strong 1750 resistance if Intel delivers a brighter outlook. Auto makers leading decliners on profit taking after recent gains, with \uc2 Hyundai Motor\uc2  (005380.SE) down 1.8% at KRW138,500, \uc2 Kia Motors\uc2  (000270.SE) down 1.7% at KRW32,400. Meanwhile, \uc2 Ssangyong Motor\uc2  (003620.SE) down 4.1% at KRW13,900 aft