elivers a brighter outlook. Auto makers leading decliners on profit taking after recent gains, with \uc2 Hyundai Motor\uc2  (005380.SE) down 1.8% at KRW138,500, \uc2 Kia Motors\uc2  (000270.SE) down 1.7% at KRW32,400. Meanwhile, \uc2 Ssangyong Motor\uc2  (003620.SE) down 4.1% at KRW13,900 after news that deadline for binding bids to buy carmaker has been extended by 3 weeks as some of 6 bidders sought more time for due diligence on Ssangyong. (jung-ah.lee@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0416 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/TWD tad down at 32.123 midday in thin trade vs 32.250 late yesterday in quiet trade, though slightly higher vs around 32.100 before usual suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  lifted pair, traders say; weak stocks (off 0.5%) and firmer USD/KRW weigh on local pair. "U.S. dollar bulls are few, while U.S. dollar bears don't dare to short" because of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , says trader at government-owned bank. Adds, KRW looks weaker today so players won't short USD in afternoon, tips pair in tight 32.090-32.150 band afternoon, and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely again to push pair higher in late session. (alex.pevzner@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0410 GMT [Dow Jones] Japan MOF sells Y2.2024 trillion of 0.4% 5-year bonds with lowest price of 100.17 yielding 0.364%, in line with market expectations. Bid-to-cover ratio at 3.37 vs 3.57 in June sale, while tail shorter at 0.01 vs 0.02 at previous tender. "As long as players continue to believe that the BOJ will keep accommodative monetary conditions for a prolonged period, there is no reason not to buy (policy-sensitive) 5-year bonds," says Daiwa Securities Capital Markets strategist Keiko Onogi. Lead September JGB futures now down 0.05 at 141.40.(megumi.fujikawa@dowjones.com) [ 07-13-10 0047ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100713e67d00038\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw1