ighlight\uc2  lifted pair, traders say; weak stocks (off 0.5%) and firmer USD/KRW weigh on local pair. "U.S. dollar bulls are few, while U.S. dollar bears don't dare to short" because of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , says trader at government-owned bank. Adds, KRW looks weaker today so players won't short USD in afternoon, tips pair in tight 32.090-32.150 band afternoon, and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely again to push pair higher in late session. (alex.pevzner@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0410 GMT [Dow Jones] Japan MOF sells Y2.2024 trillion of 0.4% 5-year bonds with lowest price of 100.17 yielding 0.364%, in line with market expectations. Bid-to-cover ratio at 3.37 vs 3.57 in June sale, while tail shorter at 0.01 vs 0.02 at previous tender. "As long as players continue to believe that the BOJ will keep accommodative monetary conditions for a prolonged period, there is no reason not to buy (policy-sensitive) 5-year bonds," says Daiwa Securities Capital Markets strategist Keiko Onogi. Lead September JGB futures now down 0.05 at 141.40.(megumi.fujikawa@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0407 GMT [Dow Jones] India government bonds down as traders tread cautiously ahead of headline inflation data for June due Wednesday, says trader with state-run bank. Benchmark 7.80% 2020 bond at 101.24 vs 101.27 last close. "The market is disappointed that there was no cut in the size of INR130 billion auction this week. Buying activity will be limited because a 25 basis point rate hike is given (at RBI's July 27 policy meeting) and tomorrow's expected higher inflation print will only reinforce that view," trader says. Tips benchmark 2020 bond in 101.10-101.40 range in session. (khushita.vasant@dowjones.com) [ 07-13-10 0047ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100713e67d00037\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
