n June sale, while tail shorter at 0.01 vs 0.02 at previous tender. "As long as players continue to believe that the BOJ will keep accommodative monetary conditions for a prolonged period, there is no reason not to buy (policy-sensitive) 5-year bonds," says Daiwa Securities Capital Markets strategist Keiko Onogi. Lead September JGB futures now down 0.05 at 141.40.(megumi.fujikawa@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0407 GMT [Dow Jones] India government bonds down as traders tread cautiously ahead of headline inflation data for June due Wednesday, says trader with state-run bank. Benchmark 7.80% 2020 bond at 101.24 vs 101.27 last close. "The market is disappointed that there was no cut in the size of INR130 billion auction this week. Buying activity will be limited because a 25 basis point rate hike is given (at RBI's July 27 policy meeting) and tomorrow's expected higher inflation print will only reinforce that view," trader says. Tips benchmark 2020 bond in 101.10-101.40 range in session. (khushita.vasant@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0402 GMT [Dow Jones] Spot gold recovers some ground in Asia on some light physical interest after dropping back through $1,200 level overnight; now at $1,199.50, up $2.40 since NY close. However, could fall later says Peter Tse, precious metals director at ScotiaMocatta in Hong Kong. "To me it feels a little bit heavy. I think we could test last week's lows between $1,185 and $1,188 later," he says. Currently few catalysts for market with EUR relatively stable vs majors; financial markets generally cautious as U.S. earnings season gets underway. (james.campbell@dowjones.com) [ 07-13-10 0043ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100713e67d00035\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
