int Stock Bank\uc2  (STB.VH) +2.4% at VND17,200, \uc2 Saigon Securities Inc\uc2 . (SSI.VH) +4.8% at VND34,700, \uc2 PetroVietnam\uc2  General Services JSC (PET.VH) +4.9% at VND25,500. Thinks index likely to reach 530 in near term. (trong-khanh.vu@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0427 GMT [Dow Jones] Nikkei turns negative in afternoon session, now down 0.3% at 9521.53 as Asian markets weaken, USD/JPY falls (now 88.44 vs 88.87 earlier, while EUR/JPY at 111.34 vs 112.07); exporters also trimming gains, notes Japanese brokerage manager. "This week's trading catalysts are short-lived," he says, citing fading excitement from \uc2 Alcoa\uc2 's (AA) strong 2Q earnings. Investor attention now shifting to Intel (INTC) as its earnings report due later in global trading day; if result cheers investors, \uc2 Tokyo Electron\uc2  (8035.TO), other chip-sensitive shares may rise tomorrow. For rest of session today, Nikkei support seen at 9500. Steel shares down on profit-taking after rising sharply yesterday on strong China trade surplus data; \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2  (5401.TO) off 1.9% at Y302. (ayai.tomisawa@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0423 GMT [Dow Jones] NZD/USD drifting back down after ticking up as high as 0.7145 earlier in session, says David Curd, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  advisor for Direct \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; "It's just sort of easing back toward the lows of the day at the moment." Pair last at 0.7118. Mood was fairly positive early, in particular after \uc2 Alcoa\uc2  kicked off U.S. earnings season on positive note; "It's been one of those risk on again stories." Weaker equity markets across much of Asia now weighing on sentiment. Tips support to hold around 0.7080, resistance at 0.7150. Says investors interested in this week's domestic data, such as retail sales, 2Q CPI but main focus on U.S. earnings. (rebecca.howard@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0423 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/CNY stays moderately higher midday in quiet trading after highe