\par\par \b \uc2 CORRECT: JGBs Fall As Stocks Rebound; Focus Shifts To Economic Fundamentals\b0\par\par\uc2 537 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 2010\par 09:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global News Select\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 ("JGBs Fall As Stocks Rebound; Focus Shifts To Economic Fundamentals," at 0627 GMT, misstated the analyst's comment in the third paragraph. The correct version follows:)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par                                      At 0600 GMT   Change \par    TFX Dec 3-Mos Euroyen Price:        99.645        flat \par    TSE Sept 10-Yr JGB Futures Price:   140.48       -0.13 \par    10-Yr 1.3% JGB No. 308 Yield:       1.215%      +0.020 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- Japanese government bonds ended lower Monday, as Tokyo share prices rebounded on hopes that China's decision to ease the yuan's peg to the dollar would improve Japan's export competitiveness.\par \par \uc2 JGBs will likely see-saw this week, as "the focus of JGB players seems to be shifting to economic fundamentals, but such cues won't be available immediately," said Keiko Onogi, senior JGB strategist at Daiwa Securities Capital Markets.\par \par \uc2 Though there may not be significant trading incentives on the economic side in coming sessions, analysts say foreign investors could sell off JGB futures if the government fails to send a clear message on fiscal reform in its roadmap to be released later this week.\par \par \uc2 Lead September JGB futures ended the day 0.13 lower at 140.48. The contract briefly moved into positive territory in the morning after the People's Bank of China unexpectedly set its yuan parity unchanged from Friday--in a sign that Beijing wants to temper expectations for sharp yuan gains in the near future.\par \par \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced over the weekend a greater degree of flexibility in the yuan's exchange rates, indicating it would allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to begin rising against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts were worried that less dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 --one of the biggest holders of U.S. government bonds--may mean less demand for U.S. Treasurys. That could put upward pressure on U.S. bond yields and indirectly affect Japan's interest rates.\par \par \uc2 Still, the benchmark 10-year cash JGB yield managed to climb 2.0 basis points to 1.215% Monday on the back of a stock recovery. The 10-year U.S. Treasury yield stood at 3.287%.\par \par \uc2 The 10-year JGB yield is likely to move in a 1.20%-1.25% range for the rest of the week, Daiwa's Onogi said.\par \par \uc2 Though the JGB market has been well-supported over the past few weeks on higher global risk-aversion, investors may not be eager to chase JGBs' upside so aggressively any more.\par \par \uc2 "The 10-year yield is unlikely to sink far below 1.2% because demand for safe-haven assets is slowing due to receding pessimism over the European sovereign debt crisis," said Jun Ishii, chief strategist at Mitsubishi UFJ Morgan Stanley Securities.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Other Cash Bond Yields            At 0600 GMT   Change \par    2-Year 0.2% JGB No. 293 Yield:          no trade \par    5-Year 0.4% JGB No. 89 Yield:       0.400%      +0.005 \par    20-Year 2.0% JGB No. 118 Yield:     1.985%      +0.015 \par    30-Year 2.3% JGB No. 32 Yield:      2.065%      +0.020 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Megumi Fujikawa, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6269-2786; megumi.fujikawa@dowjones.com [ 06-21-10 0300ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1037 4153  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020100621e66l00012\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
