\par\par \b \uc2 Taiwan dollar slips; Europe fears hit risk appetite\b0\par\par\uc2 415 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Mai 2010\par 11:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Fear of Europe debt contagion hits risk appetite\par \par \uc2 * Foreign stock selling weighs\par \par \uc2 TAIPEI, May 6 (Reuters) - The Taiwan dollar <TWD=TP> fell on Thursday, like other Asian assets a victim of mounting concerns that Greece's financial problems could trigger a sovereign debt crisis in Europe.\par \par \uc2 Taiwan stocks <.TWII> fell 1.5 percent to a two-month closing low on the concerns, further pressuring the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as risk-averse foreign investors sold a net T$12.83 billion ($406 million) of shares.\par \par \uc2 "(The Taiwan dollar) is its usual low-volatility self, but that's what we expect given pressure on stocks," said Sean Callow, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Westpac\uc2  in Australia.\par \par \uc2 "The problems aren't coming from Asia, that's the good news. The Taiwan dollar is in the same direction as everyone."\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors have sold T$43.999 billion of Taiwan shares in the month to date after total net buying of T$229.556 billion in March and April.\par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar has risen 1.2 percent this year as of Thursday, though it still lags regional peers such as the Thai baht and Korean won, largely due to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . See [EMRG/FRX] for a table of year-to-date Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  performance.\par \par \uc2 Although strategists say investor appetite in Asia could take days or weeks to recover, the Taiwan dollar is expected to gain longer term, helped by an expected revaluation in the Chinese yuan <CNY=CFXS>, for which it is a proxy, and by increases in trade and investment between Taiwan and \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The island's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still likely to step in to keep any rises orderly, however, to protect exporters, the mainstay of the economy.\par \par \uc2 A measure of non-deliverable forwards <TWDNDFOR=> indicated that investors still see the Taiwan dollar appreciating, though by less than they did the previous day.\par \par \uc2 The exchange rate in six months was seen at T$31.20 to the U.S. dollar from a view of T$30.96 the previous day, and the rate in two years T$30.14 from a previous view of T$29.89.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                             0840 GMT       PREVIOUS DAY\par  T$ (\f28 \uc2 \f2 Taipei \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 ) <TAIFX1>  31.749     31.600 (close)\par  T$ (Cosmos1) <COSMOS1>          31.680     31.512 (close)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taipei \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2  is Taiwan's main \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  exchange; Cosmos is a smaller exchange.\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-TAIWAN-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 /|LANGEN|Table|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|Z|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100509e6560004o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
