0 from NY close. Nymex May crude oil futures down 40 cents at $83.36/bbl on Globex. (philip.vahn@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0600 GMT [Dow Jones] South Korea's March inflation tamer than market forecasts, surprising economists. HI Investment & Securities economist Park Sang-hyun says prices of agricultural products likely didn't rise as much as thought despite cold weather, while price gain in global raw material prices not yet carried over to consumer prices. Economy in better-than-expected shape, but weakness in composite leading index yesterday suggests recovery will be slower in months ahead, says Park; with inflation coming below expectations, no big reason for BOK to raise rates now. Inflation to rise to lower-end of 3% in 3Q partly because government expected to raise utility fare after regional election in June; BOK likely to start tightening in December, adds Park. CPI +2.3% on year, +0.3% on month in March vs +2.6% on-year, +0.6% on-month forecasts; prices +2.7% on year, +0.4% on month in February. (kanga.kong@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0554 GMT [Dow Jones] Taiwan shares end broadly up, +1.2% at 10-week high of 8013.09, trading volume also at 10-week high of NT$138.42 billion, buoyed by gains in \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Korean bourses, possibly some government funds \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid Taiwan-\b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade pact talks in Taipei, says Hua Nan Securities Investment Management Assistant Vice President Henry Miao. "You can't let (trade pact) talks become a negative cue for the market," he says, tips Taiex support tomorrow at 5-day MA of 7943, cap around 8050. "(The trade pact) will be signed in May or June and stocks likely already reflect expectations for strong first-quarter results," he says; tips Taiex to correct to 7700 through May before trade pact signed. Construction subindex +3.2% after Economic Daily News report that Huaku Development (2548.TW) sold its residential Nangang project in only 10 days, while chip packaging, testing firms boosted by report on price hikes for 2Q: Huaku ends +4.1% to NT$85.80, Goldsun Development (2504.TW) +5.2% to NT$14.10, Advanced Semiconductor (2311.TW) +2.1% to NT$29.60; Hon Hai Precision ends +1.8% to NT$140.0 after buying 90.1% of \uc2 Sony\uc2 's Slovakia LCD TV plant. (alex.pevzner@dowjones.com) [ 04-01-10 0247ET ]\par \par \uc2 0553 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  says CNY revaluation may take place within next 3 months, earlier than previous expectation; also lowers forecast for 3-month USD/CNY NDFs to 6.74 vs 6.83 previously, 6-month NDFs to 6.66 vs 6.83 previously. "Considering the growing risks on inflation and trade protectionism, we believe China will likely benefit from an exchange rate appreciation soon," firm says. Adds, China most likely to widen daily USD/CNY trading band to 1% above or below central parity from current 0.5% band, followed by downward crawl in USD/CNY central parity; also, "a relatively small and symbolic one-off revaluation remains possible, but the likelihood of a more sizeable move remains negligible, in our view." (joy.shaw@dowjones.com) [ 04-01-10 0247ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100401e6410004r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
