aise rates now. Inflation to rise to lower-end of 3% in 3Q partly because government expected to raise utility fare after regional election in June; BOK likely to start tightening in December, adds Park. CPI +2.3% on year, +0.3% on month in March vs +2.6% on-year, +0.6% on-month forecasts; prices +2.7% on year, +0.4% on month in February. (kanga.kong@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0554 GMT [Dow Jones] Taiwan shares end broadly up, +1.2% at 10-week high of 8013.09, trading volume also at 10-week high of NT$138.42 billion, buoyed by gains in \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Korean bourses, possibly some government funds \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid Taiwan-\b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade pact talks in Taipei, says Hua Nan Securities Investment Management Assistant Vice President Henry Miao. "You can't let (trade pact) talks become a negative cue for the market," he says, tips Taiex support tomorrow at 5-day MA of 7943, cap around 8050. "(The trade pact) will be signed in May or June and stocks likely already reflect expectations for strong first-quarter results," he says; tips Taiex to correct to 7700 through May before trade pact signed. Construction subindex +3.2% after Economic Daily News report that Huaku Development (2548.TW) sold its residential Nangang project in only 10 days, while chip packaging, testing firms boosted by report on price hikes for 2Q: Huaku ends +4.1% to NT$85.80, Goldsun Development (2504.TW) +5.2% to NT$14.10, Advanced Semiconductor (2311.TW) +2.1% to NT$29.60; Hon Hai Precision ends +1.8% to NT$140.0 after buying 90.1% of \uc2 Sony\uc2 's Slovakia LCD TV plant. (alex.pevzner@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0553 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  says CNY revaluation may take place within next 3 months, earlier than previous expectation; also lowers forecast for 3-month USD/CNY NDFs to 6.74 vs 6.83 previously, 6-month NDFs to 6.66 vs 6.83 previously. "Considering the growing risks on inflation and trade protectionism, we believe China will likely benefit from an exchange rate appreciation soon," firm says. Adds, China most likely to widen daily USD/CNY trading band to 1% above or below central parity from current 0.5% band, followed by downward crawl in USD/CNY central parity; also, "a relatively small and symbolic one-off revaluation remains possible, but the likelihood of a more sizeable move remains negligible, in our view." (joy.shaw@dowjones.com) [ 04-01-10 0247ET ]\par \par \uc2 0548 GMT [Dow Jones] Taiwan government bonds end mixed in heavy volume, as better-than-expected 30-year reopened bonds auction yesterday, buying by banks offset by gains in Taiwan shares (Taiex ends +1.2%), expectations \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to buoy short-term rates higher, says local bank trader. Notes, Taiwan average interbank overnight rate climbs to multi-month high in late March. Tips bonds in tight ranges in short term on mixed short-term outlooks for bonds; "...this situation is not likely to change until results of negotiable certificates of deposit and certificates of deposit (NCDs/CDs) auction, 5-year reopened government bonds auction come out in following weeks," he says. 10-year yield ends at 1.4390% vs 1.4406%, tipped in 1.4300%-1.4400% band. In when-issued trade, 5-year yield ends at 1.0279% vs 1.0338%, eyed in 1.0100%-1.0350% band. (mason.wu@dowjones.com) [ 04-01-10 0247ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100401e6410004q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
