weeks," he says. 10-year yield ends at 1.4390% vs 1.4406%, tipped in 1.4300%-1.4400% band. In when-issued trade, 5-year yield ends at 1.0279% vs 1.0338%, eyed in 1.0100%-1.0350% band. (mason.wu@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0540 GMT [Dow Jones] JGB futures rising sharply as domestic investors buying cash bonds actively at start of Japan's new fiscal year, says Mizuho Securities market analyst Masashi Shimominami; "As JGB prices had fallen in recent days, many investors appear to be buying JGBs" at beginning of new fiscal year starting Thursday. But adds, further climbs would be limited as players likely to start taking wait-and-see attitude before release of March U.S. jobs data due Friday. Lead JGB futures at 138.64, up 0.42. 10-year yield down 3 bps at 1.360%. (tomoyuki.tachikawa@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0539 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesia's trade surplus down to $1.70 billion in February vs $2.03 billion month earlier as exports down 3.2% on month to $11.20 billion, with imports up 0.1% to $9.50 billion, the Central Statistics Agency said Thursday; surplus also below $1.85 billion median forecast from Dow Jones poll; still analysts believe lower trade surplus won't derail rupiah as capital inflows likely to continue on Indonesia's relatively sound fundamentals; (i-made.sentana@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0537 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai shares +1.9% at 802.82 at midday pause in robust trade. Energy big caps dominate activity on higher oil prices while firmer regional bourses bolster mood. Benchmark taking breather after breaking 800-psychological level, hitting almost 22-month-high at 803.29 intra-session, but sentiment still biased upward, says Finansia Syrus Securities' analyst Somchai Anektaweepon. "The rise is quite sharp, so investors start to hesitate. We may see some profit-taking that will trim gains but eventually, the index should be able to march forward." Resistance put at 810, support at 795. Among top actives, PTT Aromatics & Refining (PTTAR.TH) +3.5% at THB29.75, PTT (PTT.TH) +3.4% at THB271, \uc2 PTT Exploration & Production\uc2  (PTTEP.TH) +2.4% at THB152, \uc2 Siam Cement\uc2  (SCC.TH) +4.3% at THB268. (piyarat.setthasiriphaiboon@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0535 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/KRW extends fall despite suspected USD buying by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at around KRW1,128 earlier in day, traders say, as KRW sentiment lifted by strong Kospi (last +1.4% vs +0.8% earlier). They add, there's continued fund-inflow from overseas to local stock market. Pair last down at 1,126.9 vs 1,131.3 late yesterday in Seoul. "When dollar supply exceeds demand like this, the pair can't help it but fall," says local bank trader. Another local bank trader says, "it looks like pair could fall to as low as the 1,125-1,126 levels." But tips high chance of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by BOK below 1,125. (min-jeong.lee@dowjones.com) [ 04-01-10 0216ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100401e6410004i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
