lp it but fall," says local bank trader. Another local bank trader says, "it looks like pair could fall to as low as the 1,125-1,126 levels." But tips high chance of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by BOK below 1,125. (min-jeong.lee@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0533 GMT [Dow Jones] Taiwan's latest hike in national health insurance premium rate to have minimal impact on discretionary spending, though extra labor costs could make SMEs less inclined to pay raises, says ANZ. Premium up at 5.17%, from 4.55% of insured' monthly salaries, starting today, to replenish cash-strapped program with NT$52.2 billion annually. "We think the direct impact of the premium increases on discretionary consumer spending should be minimal, given the small incremental payments, which account for 0.1% of household disposable income," says ANZ. (crystal.hsu@dowjones.com) [ 04-01-10 0213ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100401e6410004h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
