\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korean won stable as strong stocks offset China\b0\par\par\uc2 381 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Februar 2010\par 01:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Won erases losses as stocks gain, euro edges up\par \par \uc2 * Seen staying firm; may head to early 1,140s vs dlr (Updates to domestic close)\par \par \uc2 SEOUL, Feb 16 (Reuters) - The South Korean won recovered most of its early losses on Tuesday as a rise in local stocks offset worries about the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to raise banks' reserve requirements denting risk appetite.\par \par \uc2 The won <KRW=> found further support from a firmer euro <EUR=>, which prompted investors to build up dollar-short positions.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to stay firm for the time being as Seoul shares are likely to advance further, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 But the speed of gains would be limited as caution over possible dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities emerges again, they added.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move was not new and not an interest rate hike, so it didn't cause investors to fly out of riskier assets," said Jeong My-young, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Samsung Futures Inc\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Seoul shares are expected to rise more and that will allow the won to head to the early 1,140s level (per dollar) although it is facing a resistance line at 1,147.5," she added.\par \par \uc2 The South Korean unit ended local trade at 1,151.5 versus the greenback, compared with Friday's domestic close of 1,151.3.\par \par \uc2 Initially, the won slid to as weak as 1,157.5 after the People's Bank of China said on Friday it was raising banks' reserve requirements by 50 basis points effective February 25, its second increase this year. [ID:nBJA002223]\par \par \uc2 Seoul shares <.KS11> closed up 0.46 percent as foreign investors bought a net 59.2 billion won worth of stocks on the main exchange.\par \par \uc2 The country's financial markets were closed on Monday for the Lunar New Year holidays.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                   0600 GMT      0010 GMT    prev close\par  Won               1,151.5   1,154.3/4.6       1,151.3\par  Yen/won       12.8175/277   12.8134/235   12.8199/374\par  KOSPI            1,601.05      1,595.10      1,593.66\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Cheon Jong-woo; Editing by Jonathan Hopfner)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-KOREA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100219e62g0000v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
