\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Oil Drops On China, Greece Economy Worries\b0\par\par\uc2 1,290 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Februar 2010\par 14:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in New York.  Darlene Ross, 212 416-2166; \par darlene.ross@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1321 GMT [Dow Jones] Nymex crude is trading sharply lower Friday after news that China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will raise the reserve requirement ratio for banks, stoking concerns that this could slow the country's economic growth. The lack of concrete plans from European leaders after their pledge to help debt-laden Greece Thursday is also adding to jitters in the marketplace. As traders have fled riskier assets to safer havens, the dollar has risen sharply against the euro. Oil market participants are also cautious ahead of the delayed release of key oil inventory data from the U.S. Energy Information Administration Friday morning. Nymex March crude most recently traded $1.48, or 2%, lower at $73.80/bbl. (CR)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1320 GMT [Dow Jones] Swap spreads are narrower to unchanged Friday with the 2-yr spread at 29bps from 31.05bps and the 10-yr spread where it was Thursday, at 9.75bps. Swap rates are at 1.137% and 3.802%, respectively. (DLB)\par \par \uc2 1320 GMT [Dow Jones] The Central Reserve Bank of Peru, which on Thursday left the policy rate unchanged at 1.25%, could take other moves to tighten domestic financial conditions, \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  said, pointing to slightly more hawkish language from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and to the economic recovery. "We expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to leave the policy rate unchanged at 1.25% until 2H2010 (some probability of rate hikes already during 2Q2010) and we do not rule out that before delivering rate hikes the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could elect to tighten domestic financial conditions by hiking reserve requirements (which could also act as a deterrent against foreign capital inflows and additional pressure on the PEN)." (RSK)\par \par \uc2 1317 GMT [Dow Jones] Treasurys are moderately higher across the curve early Friday. Concerns about Greece's fiscal difficulties persist, helping shorter-term Tsys especially. Tsy auctions are out of the way, but mkt has several bits of data to contend with Friday before the long holiday weekend in the U.S., for Presidents' Day. Retail sales data to come at 8:30 a.m. ET, business inventories at 10 a.m. ET and UMichigan sentiment figures at 9:55 a.m. ET. 2-yr up 2/32 to 0.851%, 10-yr up 7/32 to 3.704% and 30-yr up 12/32 to yield 4.660%. (DLB)\par \par \uc2 1310 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/USD tumbles, trading near a nine-month low, early Fri on the back of weaker-than-expected economic growth data for the euro zone and further credit tightening in China. EUR/USD was at 1.3575 from 1.3684 late Thu. (FAS)\par \par \uc2 1310 GMT [Dow Jones] EUROPEAN SUMMARY: A session packed with more woes for the Euro from weak data, a \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  tightening, suspected SNB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a sharp drop in risk appetite which hit stocks and commodities and lent government bonds support. The markets remain disappointed by the EU's response to the Greek problem and a flat reading for German 4Q GDP and miserly 0.1% 4Q growth for the euro zone did the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  little favors. The euro started to lose ground across the board prompting suspected SNB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as EUR/CHF touched a one-week low of 1.4636, the cross spiking to 1.4697. Shortly before 1000 GMT China surprised by hiking reserve requirements by 50bp in an effect to reign-in bank lending. The USD rallied hard across the board as risk appetite slumped and the euro came under further pressure. EUR/USD sank to a fresh 8-month low of 1.3532, USD/CHF rallied to a fresh 5-month high of 1.0829, GBP/USD lost over one cent to 1.5586. USD/JPY ranged between 89.60 and 90.35 while the commodity \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also took a hard knock. European government bonds are buoyed by safe-haven flows and weak data with March bunds adding 0.25 to 123.40 and March gilts 0.13 to 114.93. Peripheral EU bond spreads have widened slightly and CDS rates are on the rise once again. Equities turned negative with the main European bourses trading around par at midday, gold is $7 lower at $1086oz and oil is back under $74bbl. (GST)\par \par \uc2 1255 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 Kemet Corp\uc2 . on Thursday pulled its scheduled $275 mln 8-yr bond offering, via lead underwriter \uc2 Bank of America\uc2 Merrill Lynch\uc2 , citing market conditions, according to a person familiar with the deal, who said that ITC DeltaCom had also postponed a $325 million offer via \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2 . The high yield market has been slumping in recent weeks, and a busy calendar of new issuance earlier in the week met a tepid response, with some new notes trading below issue price in the secondary market. (MAN)\par \par \uc2 1231 GMT [Dow Jones] The UK's gilt issuance outlook looks especially worrying now that the BOE has paused its role as the bigger buyer of gilts through QE, says Neil Williams at Hermes. "With QE now on pause, looking to capital markets to fill the gap may need much higher yields. This is the last thing the Treasury needs." It may be years before the BOE starts selling its gilts back into the market, he says, adding that more QE is possible if the economy double-dips. "Until there's a credible post-election budget - probably needing headline-grabbing spending cuts - the pound just gets weaker and the gilts curve steeper." (DVC)\par \par \uc2 1215 GMT [Dow Jones] Swiss January producer and import prices are seen +0.1% on the month and -1.5% on the year, an average of four economist forecasts compiled by DJN suggests. This compares with December's +0.1% on the month and -2.5% on the year. The rise in oil prices had a positive impact on import prices, but that was to a large extent neutralized by the inability of companies to increase pricing. The data are due February 15 at 0815 GMT. (MGE)\par \par \uc2 1211 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/CZK trades at 25.950-26.005 from 25.901 late Thursday albeit down from 26.11 earlier Friday. "The koruna is pressured by disappointing 4Q GDP data releases not only here but elsewhere in Europe," \uc2 Komercni Banka\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Jan Vejmelek says. The euro may give back some its gains later Friday if US retail sales and consumer confidence data are in line with positive expectations. "I don't see the koruna weakening too much further today but next week the risk will likely be more towards weakening." Vejmelek notes uncertainties over Greece remain in focus. (LEO)\par \par \uc2 1153 GMT [Dow Jones] Bunds ease off their highs Friday but mostly hold gains after spiking earlier in the session on weak euro zone GDP and industrial production data. The focus now turns to US retail sales at 1330 GMT and Michigan consumer sentiment at 1455 GMT. The March bund futures contract is currently up 0.24 on the day at 123.39, within a 123.10-123.51 range. The 10-year benchmark bund is up 0.31 at 100.40, yielding 3.201%. (DVC)\par \par \uc2 1144 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/JPY's trend-channel high coincides with the 21 and 60 DMA's near 90.30, and this level is expected to cap, says \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2 . Now at 90.01 from the day's high of 90.36, BarCap is looking for a return to 89.00 and a possible retest of the 88.55 low. Only a daily close above 90.60 would prove this view incorrect, says the bank. (GST) [ 02-12-10 0822ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100212e62c00085\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw145\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2175\pichgoal600
