\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Slides in rupiah, peso trigger c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 748 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Januar 2010\par 09:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Rupiah, peso turn lower on \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  tightening jitters\par \par \uc2 * Falling rupiah, peso prompt c.banks to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Won at 4-week low on \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dollar/Won NDFs jump\par \par \uc2 By Kevin Yao\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Jan 26 (Reuters) - Central banks in Indonesia and the Philippines \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness on Tuesday after \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  implemented a rise in bank reserve requirements to curb lending, raising fears that Asia's rapid economic recovery might suffer.\par \par \uc2 Banking sources said several banks, which were selected by the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise their reserve ratios for excessive lending, will see these measures take effect on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The moves follow other steps imposed by policymakers recently to curb credit growth and drain liquidity to prevent the economy from overheating.[ID:nBJD003445]\par \par \uc2 China's strong rebound from the global slowdown has helped buoy neighbouring Asian economies and their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent months, offsetting the impact of still weak demand in the region's traditional Western export markets.\par \par \uc2 The yen, meanwhile, gave up most of its early gains after \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  cut its outlook on Japan's long-term sovereign debt rating. [ID:nTKW006776]\par \par \uc2 S&P's move had little impact on emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which were most down versus the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 RUPIAH, PESO\par \par \uc2 Indonesian rupiah <IDR=> opened firmer at 9,300 per dollar on a brief rise in investors' risk appetite but later turned sharply lower and forced the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  The rupiah fell to 9,440 per dollar -- down about 1 percent\par from Monday's close -- after hitting its intraday high of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 9,280.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We suspect \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  selling at high today at 9,440," said a Jakarta-based trader.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Rupiah strengthened in the morning but is now being sold off. We have lots of custodian clients buying dollars at the moment," said the trader.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 One-month dollar/rupiah NDFs <IDRNDFOR=> shot up to 9,480 from Monday's close at 9,370.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine peso <PHP=> ended local trading at 46.595 per dollar, 0.8 percent weaker than the previous close.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We got BSP (the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) well placed on the offer," said a trader in Manila.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 WON\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The won <KRW=> opened firmer at 1,146 per dollar but was later knocked down by China's implementation of the higher reserve requirements, falling just over 1 percent to 1,165.9 -- its lowest in four weeks.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The won came under further pressure after data showed the economy lost its recovery momentum in the fourth quarter last year. [ID:nTOE60O00L]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Charts point to further weakness in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . [ID:nSGE60O0AT]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dollar/won NDFs <KRWNDFOR=> jumped across the curve as some investors, including hedge funds, were forced to cover short dollar positions to stop losses.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 One-month NDFs rise sharply to 1,166.5 after opening at 1,146.5.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Funds caught short this round are all dead -- quite a few funds sold dollar/won below 1,150 level," says a NDF Singapore-based trader.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sporadic dollar selling started to emerge after 1-month NDFs hit the high but the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remained biddish, traders said. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day at   0822 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        90.06          90.23       +0.19\par  Sing dlr        1.4040         1.3984       -0.40\par  Taiwan dlr      32.045         31.970       -0.23\par  Korean won     1161.40        1150.00       -0.98\par  Baht             33.00          32.95       -0.15\par  Peso             46.66          46.24       -0.91\par  Rupiah         9390.00        9310.00       -0.85\par  Rupee            46.12          46.12       +0.00\par  Ringgit         3.4200         3.3995       -0.60\par  Yuan            6.8270         6.8269       -0.00\par  Change so far in 2010\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        90.06          92.90       +3.15\par  Sing dlr        1.4040         1.4053       +0.09\par  Taiwan dlr      32.045         32.030       -0.05\par  Korean won     1161.40        1164.50       +0.27\par  Baht             33.00          33.32       +0.97\par  Peso             46.66          46.20       -0.99\par  Rupiah         9390.00        9420.00       +0.32\par  Rupee            46.12          46.54       +0.90\par  Ringgit         3.4200         3.4220       +0.06\par  Yuan            6.8270         6.8270       +0.00\par \f28 \par \p