\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar eases as China liquidity concerns linger\b0\par\par\uc2 490 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 2010\par 08:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Jan 14 (Reuters) - The following is a snapshot of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money market on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                            Latest           Previous Day\par                            At 0553 GMT      At 0553 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>           7.7567/69        7.7551/52\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month <HKD3M=>    -51.50/-47.50       -50/-46\par  Six-month <HKD6M=>     -102.50/-92.50      -102/-94\par  One-year <HKD1Y=>         -215/-205        -210/-200\par  INTERBANK RATES (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight <HKDOND=>       0.01/0.15     0.00001/0.03\par  One-month <HKD1MD=>       0.02/0.11        0.01/0.06\par  Three-month <HKD3MD=>     0.03/0.33        0.07/0.12\par  Six-month <HKD6MD=>       0.07/0.34        0.20/0.24\par  One-year <HKD1YD=>        0.60/1.00        0.50/0.55\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 For more live quotes of forwards and interbank rates, click on <HKDF=>.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar weakened against the U.S. dollar on Thursday with UK and U.S. banks buying U.S. dollars, traders said. China's move this week to raise bank reserve requirements continued to put pressure on the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as tighter Chinese monetary policy could curb capital inflows to the territory from the mainland, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 * The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <HKD=> was quoted at 7.7566/68 versus the U.S. dollar at 0633 GMT, having earlier hit a session low of 7.7570.\par \par \uc2 * Analysts said the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also depressed by a rally this year in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that are not pegged to the dollar, such as the Indonesian rupiah <IDR=>, which are benefiting from rising risk appetite as the global economy shows signs of improving.\par \par \uc2 * Traders expect the Hong Kong dollar to trade in a range between 7.7550 and 7.7585 in the next two weeks.\par \par \uc2 * Hong Kong attracted a record HK$640 billion (US$83 billion) in fund inflows between October 2008 and December 2009, much of it from mainland \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  and forcing massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar is pegged at 7.80 to the U.S. dollar but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85. Under the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg, the HKMA is obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hits 7.75 or 7.85 to keep the band intact.\par \par \uc2 * Local interbank rates were trapped in a narrow range on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Three-month Hibor <HIHKD3MD=> was fixed at 0.12000 percent, unchanged from Wednesday. One-year Hibor <HIHKD1YD=> softened to 0.05964 percent from 0.06000 percent the previous day.\par \par \uc2 MARKET/ECONOMIC NEWS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  > Stock market reports and updates:                       [.HK]\par  > Yuan reports and updates:                              [CNY/]\par  > U.S. dollar reports and updates:                [USD/] [FRX/]\par  > Emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports and updates:           [EMRG/FRX]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Susan Fenton; Editing by Chris Lewis)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-HONGKONG/FORWARDS|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|O|OIL|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|Z|ABX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PCM|PEN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100117e61e00036\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppi