\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea won at over 15-mth high on US,  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2  data\b0\par\par\uc2 464 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 2010\par 01:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Exporters support \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  further despite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  * Seen stronger on rising recovery hopes  (Updates to domestic close)\par \par \uc2  By Cheon Jong-woo\par \par \uc2  SEOUL, Jan 11 (Reuters) - The South Korean won hit a fresh over 15-month high against the dollar on Monday as disappointing U.S. job data dampened the greenback and healthy China trade figures bolstered hopes for an economic recovery.\par \par \uc2  The won <KRW=> found further support from exporters' demand for settlements, although the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities were spotted buying dollars to contain the won's rise, traders said.\par \par \uc2  The authorities were seen trying to prevent the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from ending local trade stronger than 1,200 per dollar, but surging dollar offers from exporters made the attempt fail, traders added.\par \par \uc2  The South Korean unit is expected to stay firm as evidence of a recovery in Asia's fourth-largest economy is likely to keep attracting foreign funds, analysts said.\par \par \uc2  Expectations of an early interest rate raise by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  have eased, but the Bank of Korea is still expected to increase interest rates earlier than the United States, they added.\par \par \uc2  "Investors are looking for risky assets and Korea seems to be the best place to get stable profits. That will push up the won to 1,100 per dollar in the short term," said Kim Jae-eun, an economist at \uc2 Hyundai Securities\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  The won rose almost 1 percent to end at 1,119.8 versus the dollar from Friday's domestic close <KRW=KFTC> of 1,130.5.\par \par \uc2  The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed to as strong as 1,117.5, the strongest since Sept. 22, 2008.\par \par \uc2  U.S. companies cut 85,000 jobs in December, data showed on Friday, confounding expectations that the labor market was finally stabilizing [ID:nN0747110]\par \par \uc2  Growth in China's exports and imports last month blew past expectations, providing fresh evidence of the vigour of South Korea's top exports market. [ID:nSGE60A016]\par \par \uc2  On the corporate front, \uc2 Daewoo Shipbuilding & Marine Engineering\uc2   said on Saturday it had won orders totalling $750 million, prompting expectations for more won demand. [ID:nTOE60800S]\par \par \uc2  Seoul shares <.KS11> ended down 0.07 percent as foreign investors sold a net 160.7 billion won worth of stocks on the main exchange.\par \par \uc2  Foreigners purchased a combined net 1.57 trillion won during the previous seven consecutive sessions.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                   0605 GMT      0005 GMT    prev close\par  Won               1,119.8  1,119.9/20.6       1,130.5\par  Yen/won       12.1258/528   12.1354/463   12.1099/177\par  KOSPI            1,694.12      1,700.49      1,695.26\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  (Additional reporting by Lee Kyoung-ho; Editing by Jonathan\par Hopfner)\par \par \par \par \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-KOREA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100114e61b0000w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
