\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar stays on the strong side, Hibors ease\b0\par\par\uc2 682 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 November 2009\par 07:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Nov 17 (Reuters) - The following is a snapshot of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money market on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                            Latest           Previous Day\par                            At 0602 GMT      At 0643 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>           7.7500/01        7.7500/01\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month <HKD3M=>       -50/-47          -50/-47\par  Six-month <HKD6M=>        -110/-105        -114/-104\par  One-year <HKD1Y=>         -247/-237        -252/-243\par  INTERBANK RATES (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight <HKDOND=>       0.001/0.05       0.005/0.05\par  One-month <HKD1MD=>       0.06/0.09        0.06/0.10\par  Three-month <HKD3MD=>     0.10/0.14        0.10/0.15\par  Six-month <HKD6MD=>       0.30/0.35        0.30/0.36\par  One-year <HKD1YD=>        0.51/0.61        0.60/0.64\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 For more live quotes of forwards and interbank rates, click on <HKDF=>.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar continued to trade at the top of its trading band on Tuesday, but there was no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the city's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in New York trade on Monday after the Hong Kong government pledged to keep its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pegged to the U.S. dollar and said it would not change its trading band.\par \par \uc2 The HKMA told Reuters on Monday that the pegged system was "well equipped" to cope with capital inflows and that it would not re-peg or widen the Hong Kong dollar's trading band even if China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciated. Hong Kong chief executive Donald Tsang, speaking in Singapore on Monday, said the peg had served Hong Kong well over the past two decades and it would stay as long as he is in office. Tsang's term will end in 2012. [ID:nSP375168]\par \par \uc2 * Dealers said the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) did not need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  because a recent inflow of funds to subscribe to \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  Minsheng Bank\uc2 's IPO was slowing down.\par \par \uc2 Minsheng's offering is nearing its end and the shares will list in Hong Kong stock market on Nov. 26.\par \par \uc2 But one dealer at a local bank expected the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <HKD=> to remain strong as investors would continue to park money in higher-yielding assets and emerging markets, with the U.S. dollar continuing to lose ground and U.S. interest rates likely to stay low for some time.\par \par \uc2 * Funds have been pouring into Hong Kong assets in recent months, pushing the Hong Kong dollar to the top of its trading band, prompting the HKMA to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  actively.\par \par \uc2 The HKMA stressed on Monday that any appreciation of the Chinese yuan <CNY=CFXS> would not lead to an adjustment in the Hong Kong dollar \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg.\par \par \uc2 From October to Nov. 16, the HKMA has injected more than HK$164 billion into the territory's banking system to defend the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  peg, lifting the aggregate balance -- a measure of\par interbank liquidity -- to HK$306.365 billion.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * The Hong Kong dollar is pegged at 7.80 to the U.S. dollar but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85. The HKMA is usually obliged to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  when the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hits 7.75 or 7.85.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Local interbank rates remain at a low level because of abundant liquidity in the banking system.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Three-month Hibor <HIHKD3MD=> was fixed at 0.13893 percent, its lowest level since April, 2004, and was down from Monday's 0.14929 percent.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * A dealer at a European bank said Hong Kong dollar interest rate swaps (IRS) fell on Tuesday, tracking lower U.S. bond yields overnight after Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke repeated the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's pledge of keeping rates near zero to sustain economic growth.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * The Hong Kong government will release unemployment data for August-October at 0830 GMT.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MARKET/ECONOMIC NEWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  > Stock market reports and updates:                       [.HK]\par  > Yuan reports and updates:                              [CNY/]\par  > U.S. dollar reports and updates:                [USD/] [FRX/]\par  > Emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports and updates:           [EMRG/FRX]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Christina Lo; Editing by Jonathan Hopfner)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-HONGKONG/FORWARDS|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|O|OIL|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|Z|ABX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PCM|PEN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091120e5bh000fs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
