\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2  Yuan Ends Up; \highlight22\uc2 FX Interventions \highlight\uc2  In Asia Cap Gains\b0\par\par\uc2 544 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Oktober 2009\par 11:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds closing levels)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                                   Vs Parity    Pvs \par USD/CNY Central Parity   6.8270               6.8290 \par USD/CNY OTC 0930 GMT     6.8256    -0.02%     6.8263 \par              High        6.8275    +0.01% \par              Low         6.8252    -0.03% \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI (Dow Jones)--China's yuan ended slightly higher against the dollar Friday, the first day of trading after the National Day holiday, taking its cue from the U.S. unit's broad weakness on global markets in the past week.\par \par \uc2 However, dollar purchases by Asian central banks as they sought to limit strength in their own \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  curbed the yuan's gains.\par \par \uc2 On the over-the-counter market, the dollar ended at CNY6.8256, down from CNY6.8263 Sept. 30, the last trading day before China's week-long holiday. It traded between CNY6.8252 and CNY6.8275.\par \par \uc2 During China's holiday, the dollar fell sharply against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to an expected interest rate hike by Australia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , rising gold prices and better-than-expected economic data globally.\par \par \uc2 Late Thursday, the dollar was at Y88.41, down from Y89.75 Sept. 30, the Australian dollar was at US$0.9060, up from US$0.8834 over the same period, and the euro was up at $1.4789 from $1.4635.\par \par \uc2 The dollar recovered some of its recent losses against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia on Friday after Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke reiterated the U.S. will need to raise interest rates once the recovery takes hold.\par \par \uc2 But local dealers remain bearish about the dollar, saying it may fall to CNY6.8200 before the end of the year, citing ultra-low U.S. interest rates.\par \par \uc2 "China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to rein in the yuan's rise against the dollar through the central parity rate, so traders didn't sell the dollar aggressively during the session," said a Shanghai-based trader at a foreign bank.\par \par \uc2 The People's Bank of China\uc2  set the dollar-yuan central parity rate at 6.8270 Friday, down from 6.8290 on Sept. 30.\par \par \uc2 "The dollar's decline against the yuan was also capped by Asian central banks' \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the U.S. unit," said another Shanghai-based trader at a European bank.\par \par \uc2 Asian monetary authorities, including central banks in South Korea, Taiwan, the Philippines, Thailand and Hong Kong, have been seeking to temper rallies in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it sold HK$3.88 billion Thursday to defend the Hong Kong dollar's peg to the U.S. dollar. The \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  also confirmed it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but didn't elaborate.\par \par \uc2 "But bearish sentiment for the dollar will continue, as most developed countries are expected to maintain their loose monetary polices in the remaining months of the year so the U.S. Fed is unlikely to raise the U.S. interest rate in the short term," said the trader at the European bank.\par \par \uc2 Offshore, one-year dollar-yuan nondeliverable forwards were at 6.6791/6.6831, down from 6.6970/6.7020 on Sept. 30.\par \par \uc2 -Rose Yu contributed to this article, Dow Jones Newswires; 8621 6120-1200; rose.yu@dowjones.com [ 09-10-09 0935GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1153   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020091009e5a9000sv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
