\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar stays strong, interbank rates slip\b0\par\par\uc2 515 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Mai 2009\par 06:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, May 14 (Reuters) - The following is a snapshot of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money markets on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                        Morning     Previous Close\par                        At 0339 GMT At 0843 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>       7.7501/02   7.7504/05\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month <HKD3M=>   -71/-65     -68/-62\par  Six-month <HKD6M=>    -106/-98     -98/-92\par  One-year <HKD1Y=>     -154/-139   -142/-132\par  INTERBANK RATES (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight <HKDOND=> 0.0001/0.0001 0.0001/0.0001\par  One-month <HKD1MD=>   0.02/0.10   0.03/0.07\par  Three-month <HKD3MD=> 0.30/0.45   0.30/0.45\par  Six-month <HKD6MD=>   0.60/0.80   0.70/0.83\par  One-year <HKD1YD=>    1.11/1.21   1.15/1.25\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 * For more live quotes for forwards and interbank rates, click on <FWEN>.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar stayed close to its upper trading band against the U.S. dollar on Thursday, while interbank rates extended their decline after another liquidity injection by the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) overnight.\par \par \uc2 * The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <HKD=> was trading at 7.7501 at 0349 GMT, having earlier hit a session low of 7.7508, hovering just a whisker from its upper limit at 7.7500 against the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 Dealers expect the spot to trade narrowly in the near term, with attention focusing on fund flows and stock market performance.\par \par \uc2 * Hong Kong stocks <.HSI><.HSCE> retreated on Thursday after dismal U.S. retail sales data damped confidence in a recovery in the world's largest economy.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar has been boosted by capital inflows into the territory over the past month on signs that \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy is recovering.\par \par \uc2 * The HKMA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Wednesday and sold HK$3.1 billion ($400 million) for U.S. dollars during New York trading hours to stem the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreciation and keep it within its trading band. [ID:nHKG315365]\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will lift the aggregate balance -- the sum of balances on clearing accounts maintained by banks with the HKMA -- to a record HK$249.192 billion by May 15 when the transaction is settled.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is pegged at 7.80 to the U.S. dollar but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85. Under the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg, the HKMA is usually obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the Hong Kong dollar hits 7.75 or 7.85 to keep the band intact.\par \par \uc2 * Local interbank rates extended their fall and the discount on Hong Kong dollar forwards widened on Thursday amid abundant liquidity in the banking system.\par \par \uc2 Three-month Hibor <HIHKD3MD=> was fixed at 0.55214 percent, its lowest level since January 5, 2005 and down from Wednesday's 0.62857 percent.\par \par \uc2 MARKET/ECONOMIC NEWS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  > Stock market reports and updates:                       [.HK]\par  > Yuan reports and updates:                              [CNY/]\par  > U.S. dollar reports and updates:                [USD/] [FRX/]\par  > Emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports and updates:           [EMRG/FRX]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Christina Lo; Editing by Chris Lewis)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-HONGKONG/FORWARDS|LANGEN|Table|Z